The implementation path matches the intended ordering so far: classification happens before duplicate tracking, headers never reach entry parsing or `_known_of`, and physical positions come from `enumerate()` over all file lines—including unreadable/skipped lines. One nuance I’m testing explicitly is that “byte-identical” is implemented on stripped line text, which is slightly broader than raw-byte identity; that can only force verification/refusal, but I’ll check whether any normal writer transformation makes it operationally relevant.
